# Fishhawk local-dev environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in the values you need:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The Makefile auto-includes .env if present, so `make dev-backend`
# picks these up without `set -a; source .env; set +a` plumbing.
#
# `fishhawkd` ignores any variable that isn't set, but it logs a
# warning on startup for each missing piece (OAuth, webhooks, etc.).
# See docs/github-app/README.md for the local-dev modes that
# determine which of these you need.

# --- core (required) ---

# Postgres connection string. Matches docker-compose.yml.
FISHHAWKD_DATABASE_URL=postgres://fishhawk:fishhawk@localhost:5432/fishhawk?sslmode=disable

# Listen address. Defaults to :8080 if unset; uncomment to override.
# FISHHAWKD_ADDR=:8080

# --- opt-in local TLS front end (E66.28 / #2453) ---
# OFF by default. Set FISHHAWK_DEV_TLS=1 to make `scripts/dev up` add a
# loopback-only caddy reverse proxy that terminates TLS on :8443 in front of the
# unmodified plain-http fishhawkd, so the OAuth 2.1 AS can be exercised over
# https on a workstation. Requires `brew install caddy` (or point
# FISHHAWK_DEV_TLS_PROXY_BIN at the binary). See docs/local-tls.md for the
# client-trust (NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS) step -- NOT sufficient on its own for
# first-time MCP OAuth, see the one-time bootstrap and the tunnel
# alternative in that doc -- the AS config recipe and the audience-port
# foot-gun. Only the literal 1 enables it.
# FISHHAWK_DEV_TLS=1
# FISHHAWK_DEV_TLS_PORT=8443
# FISHHAWK_DEV_TLS_PROXY_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin/caddy

# --- local k8s port-forward host ports (E69.6 / #2917) ---
# `scripts/dev k8s` forwards three HOST ports to the in-cluster Services. Each
# is overridable so a host where something already holds 8080 (or 16686/4318)
# can still run the local bring-up. Only the HOST side moves; the in-cluster
# side is chart-owned.
#
# EMPTY MEANS DEFAULT: these use the same `${VAR:-default}` derivation as every
# other knob in scripts/dev, so `FISHHAWK_K8S_PF_PORT=` resolves to 8080 rather
# than to an empty port. A non-numeric, zero, negative or >65535 value is
# rejected with a diagnostic naming the variable and the range (1..65535)
# before kubectl is invoked. The two JAEGER ports must also DIFFER from each
# other: one host port cannot carry both mappings, so setting them equal (even
# to a free port) makes `scripts/dev k8s` skip the jaeger forward with a warning
# naming both variables — fishhawkd still comes up, tracing does not.
#
# CAVEAT: values-local.yaml pins config.oauthCallbackUrl to
# http://localhost:8080/v0/auth/github/callback, so a non-default
# FISHHAWK_K8S_PF_PORT needs a matching
# `--set config.oauthCallbackUrl=http://localhost:<port>/v0/auth/github/callback`
# for GitHub sign-in to complete. `scripts/dev k8s` prints the exact line.
# FISHHAWK_K8S_PF_PORT=8080
# FISHHAWK_K8S_JAEGER_UI_PORT=16686
# FISHHAWK_K8S_JAEGER_OTLP_PORT=4318

# --- opt-in local webhook relay (E64.49 / #3169) ---
# OFF by default. Set FISHHAWK_DEV_WEBHOOK_RELAY=1 to make `scripts/dev up` start
# a smee.io client that forwards GitHub App deliveries from your channel to
# POST /webhooks/github on the local fishhawkd, so the webhook-driven behaviours
# work locally. The channel is STRICTLY per-developer with NO committed default:
# pointing the single App at your channel REDIRECTS its deliveries away from any
# other consumer. Create one at https://smee.io/new. Requires
# `npm install -g smee-client` (or point FISHHAWK_DEV_SMEE_BIN at the binary).
# Only the literal 1 enables it. The relay COEXISTS with the merge reconciler
# (FISHHAWKD_ENABLE_MERGE_RECONCILER, off by default) deliberately — the
# reconciler's heal is idempotent and the publisher dedups, so they are
# belt-and-braces, not a race. See docs/local-webhook-relay.md.
# FISHHAWK_DEV_WEBHOOK_RELAY=1
# FISHHAWK_DEV_WEBHOOK_CHANNEL=
# FISHHAWK_DEV_SMEE_BIN=/opt/homebrew/bin/smee-client

# --- acceptance preview least-privilege role (E31.19 / #1577) ---
# `scripts/dev preview` runs the UNTRUSTED merge-candidate binary against a
# throwaway <dbname>_preview database using a dedicated non-superuser role —
# NOT the operator credential above — that owns only that database and is denied
# CONNECT to the dev database. Defaults below; override only if the default
# role name/password collides on a shared Postgres. An overridden password MUST
# be URL-safe (it is spliced into the preview DATABASE_URL).
# FISHHAWK_PREVIEW_DB_ROLE=fishhawk_preview
# FISHHAWK_PREVIEW_DB_PASSWORD=fishhawk_preview

# --- preview OAuth AS passthrough (E66.36 / #2473) ---
# `scripts/dev preview` forwards EXACTLY these three FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_* keys
# from this file onto the preview's serve exec line — nothing else, and
# nothing inherited wholesale from your shell. Set them (see the AS config
# recipe in docs/local-tls.md) to make the preview's /v0/oauth/* routes
# answer non-503, so an acceptance run can validate OAuth AS behaviour.
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_ISSUER must be an https origin — no http escape hatch
# (RFC 8414 §2 grants no loopback exemption).
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_ISSUER=https://localhost:8443
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_RESOURCE=https://localhost:8443/mcp
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_REQUIRE_LOOPBACK=true

# --- background workers ---
# Off by default so dev runs aren't racing the timer/watchdog.

# FISHHAWKD_ENABLE_SLA_TIMER=true
# FISHHAWKD_ENABLE_DISPATCH_WATCHDOG=true

# --- GitHub App (Mode B / C in docs/github-app/README.md) ---
# Without these, /webhooks/github responds 503 and dispatch is disabled.

# FISHHAWKD_GITHUB_APP_ID=123456
# FISHHAWKD_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY_FILE=/path/to/private-key.pem
# FISHHAWKD_GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...

# --- OAuth sign-in (Mode B / C) ---
# All three must be set together; mismatch fails fast.
# Without these, /v0/auth/github/* responds 503.

# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=Iv1.xxxx
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:8080/v0/auth/github/callback
# Post-login redirect target. ONLY A RELATIVE PATH PASSES VALIDATION —
# isSafeRelativeRedirect (backend/internal/server/auth.go) rejects anything
# whose first character is not '/', and any value carrying a scheme or host,
# as an open-redirect vector. An absolute URL here is SILENTLY discarded and
# the redirect falls back to '/'. In the split-origin dev layout the SPA is
# reached through Vite's proxy, so a relative path is what you want anyway.
# FISHHAWKD_OAUTH_REDIRECT_AFTER_LOGIN=/

# --- SPA root for back-links (#231) ---
# Used as `details_url` on the published `fishhawk_audit_complete`
# GitHub Check Run so a reviewer who clicks the check on github.com
# lands on the run page in Fishhawk. Vite serves the SPA on :5173 in
# local dev. Empty disables the publish-to-GitHub path cleanly; the
# in-Fishhawk gate enforcement still works.

# FISHHAWKD_EXTERNAL_URL=http://localhost:5173

# --- runner OIDC (only when iterating on the signing-key endpoint) ---
# Off by default — endpoint accepts any caller (v0 self-execution
# posture). Set to a non-empty audience to enforce verification.

# FISHHAWKD_OIDC_AUDIENCE=fishhawkd-local
# FISHHAWKD_OIDC_JWKS_URL=https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com/.well-known/jwks

# --- trace storage (S3 / RustFS) ---
# Without FISHHAWKD_S3_BUCKET, POST /v0/runs/{id}/trace responds 503 and
# every run fails at trace upload AFTER the agent has run and been billed.
# docker-compose.yml ships a RustFS (S3-compatible) instance on :9000.
# `scripts/dev up --start-deps` (and `reload`/`post-merge --start-deps`)
# wires it AUTOMATICALLY when NONE of the five variables below is set in
# .env or the shell: it creates the bucket (the same idempotent command as
# `make s3-init`) and exports exactly these five values to fishhawkd.
# Uncomment them only for a non-default bucket/endpoint or a real S3 store.
# Setting ANY one of them (including AWS_* credentials held for another
# purpose) makes scripts/dev leave all five untouched — it never overwrites
# an operator value — so then set the whole block here yourself.

# FISHHAWKD_S3_BUCKET=fishhawk-traces
# FISHHAWKD_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# FISHHAWKD_S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=fishhawk
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=fishhawk-dev-secret

# Dev-only escape hatch (E45.76 / #3601): with FISHHAWKD_S3_BUCKET unset,
# select an in-memory trace store so the trace route is drivable. It mounts
# NO dev surface, so the daemon is NOT in dev mode and forge writes stay live.
# The store is EPHEMERAL: every trace bundle is lost when fishhawkd restarts,
# so this is not a substitute for the durable block above.
# FISHHAWKD_DEV_FIXTURES is NOT the trace-store remedy: it yields the same
# in-memory store but ALSO puts the daemon in dev mode, which DENIES every
# forge write (no branch push, no PR/MR) and refuses host-dispatch.
# FISHHAWKD_DEV_TRACE_STORE=true

# --- OTel trace export (opt-in, #649/#679) ---
# The runner emits a per-run GenAI trace (a `stage <name>` span with a
# `chat <model>` child carrying gen_ai.* + fishhawk.* cost/repro attrs)
# ONLY when OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT is set; unset is a clean no-op,
# so the default loop is unaffected (runner gates emission on this var,
# runner/internal/otelemit/otelemit.go).
#
# http://localhost:4318 points at the compose `otel`-profile Jaeger
# (`docker compose --profile otel up -d`); view traces at
# http://localhost:16686.
#
# CAVEAT: the endpoint must be reachable from wherever the runner
# ACTUALLY executes. The standard dogfood loop dispatches the runner to
# a GitHub-hosted CI runner, where `localhost:4318` is the CI host's
# loopback — NOT this machine. End-to-end local viewing therefore
# requires the runner to run on a host that can reach this collector
# (invoke fishhawk-runner locally). See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §10
# (local OTLP collector row) for the verification path.

# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318

# --- plan review (ADR-027) ---
# Per-invocation timeout for plan/implement review agent calls. The code
# default is 300s (#606) — sized to cover review of large standard_v1 plans.
# Leave this commented to inherit that default. Setting a value BELOW 300s
# risks timing out large plans (the reviewer is killed mid-review and the
# stage records a *_review_failed audit entry); fishhawkd logs a startup WARN
# if the effective value is under the 300s floor.
# FISHHAWKD_PLAN_REVIEW_TIMEOUT=300s

# --- single-tenant deployment profile (ADR-057 Mode 1, E44.9 / #1833) ---
# The multi-tenant core admits a sign-in only against an EXISTING accounts row,
# and nothing creates that first row — so a fresh self-host has no admitting
# account until this profile bootstraps one at startup. Every member of the
# configured enterprise / org / group (or, for `user` granularity, the owner
# themselves) then auto-joins through the normal login gate.
#
# ENABLEMENT: FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_ACCOUNT_KEY alone enables the profile.
# Every variable below defaults to EMPTY; the github / enterprise / member
# defaults are applied INTERNALLY, only after the key enables the profile.
# Setting ANY other SINGLE_TENANT variable while the account key is empty is a
# startup error (fishhawkd refuses to boot rather than silently degrade to
# hosted mode). Leave the whole block commented for hosted multi-tenant.
#
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_ACCOUNT_KEY=acme-corp     # enterprise slug / org login / group path; SOLE enablement signal
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_GRANULARITY=enterprise    # enterprise | organization | group | user (default: enterprise once the key is set)
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_AUTO_JOIN_ROLE=member     # role auto-joining members get (default: member; an empty role admits nobody)
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_DISPLAY_NAME=             # cosmetic; empty stores NULL
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_PROVIDER=github           # github | gitlab (default: github once the key is set)
#
# Personal-namespace (single-developer) self-host: set GRANULARITY=user and the
# ACCOUNT KEY to your OWN forge login, matched BYTE-EXACTLY (no case
# normalization — a casing mismatch denies you on the first sign-in). The
# `user` tier admits with NO live forge membership read.
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_GRANULARITY=user
# FISHHAWKD_SINGLE_TENANT_ACCOUNT_KEY=octocat
#
# Full operator guide, troubleshooting, and the denial-log fields:
# docs/deploy/self-hosted.md
